  "OverallSummary": "This case involves The Jeffrey Matthews Financial Group, L.L.C. (JMFG), a full-service broker-dealer primarily conducting a municipal securities business. From June 30, 2020, until March 2023, JMFG failed to establish, maintain, and enforce written policies and procedures reasonably designed to achieve compliance with Regulation Best Interest (Reg BI) and its Form CRS obligations. The firm's WSPs had a section titled Reg BI but contained no actual policies or procedures regarding compliance with Reg BI requirements. Additionally, JMFG's training on Reg BI was inadequate, focusing on suitability rather than Reg BI requirements. Similarly, JMFG's WSPs regarding Form CRS lacked specific procedures for preparing, filing, or updating Form CRS. The case does not identify specific Care Obligation violations or individual customer impacts, but rather addresses systemic failures in the firm's compliance framework. The violations were at the firm-level concerning compliance procedures, resulting in a censure and a $35,000 fine ($17,500 of which pertains to MSRB Rule G-27 violations). After FINRA identified these issues, JMFG revised its WSPs beginning in March 2023 to provide guidance regarding Reg BI and Form CRS and implemented proper training on Reg BI for its representatives."
